Done.

**Reproduced** — `./target/debug/rb run` on `set name to "Bob"` / `say "Hello, {name}!"` printed `Hello, {name}!`, exit 0; `grep -n InterpolatedText src/parser.rs` printed one line.

**Fixed** — `src/parser.rs` now constructs `Expr::InterpolatedText` from the text arm of `parse_primary`. A `{` starts a substitution only when it has a matching `}` whose contents read as one whole expression; an unmatched `{`, a lone `}`, `{}`, a JSON document, or `{1 + }` stay literal, and a literal with no substitution is still one `Expr::Text`. Both engines, the analyzer, the formatter and the linter now run for real.

**Follow-through the change forced** — `bootstrap/compiler.rb` learned the same rule so stage2 stays byte-identical to stage 1 (S3 fixed point green); the two corpus goldens, the wasm `HELLO` constant and the documented bytecode instruction sequence for `say "n is {1 + 2}"` were updated to the correct values; `tests/test_text.rb:37` and `:138`, which pinned the broken behaviour, were corrected rather than deleted.

**Gates** — `cargo fmt --all -- --check` clean, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean, `cargo test --all-targets` 1391 passed / 0 failed / 0 ignored. `./rbops/verify.sh` **was not run** — there is no `rbops/` directory in this checkout and the contract forbids inspecting the pipeline elsewhere; what it covers was run by hand (all 9 files in `examples/` and `modules/` exit 0, plus `edge_project_tests_directory_has_no_failures`). `phases/phase-047/REPORT.md` records that honestly rather than claiming a pass.

**Known gap** — `interp_depth`'s limit branch is unreachable through the current grammar (the outer lexer resolves escapes, so an inner source containing a string literal cannot re-lex to itself); no test pins that branch, and `FINDINGS.md` says why and what a real phase would do about it.

DONE
